    "detailed_description": "Throwing Master is a casual competitive game played by two to four players, who make decisions based on the rules of the game and choose their preferred weapon to defeat their opponent.<br><br>- Requires at least 2-4 players to play.<br><br>- Players set the rules of the game, choose the scene to fight.<br><br>- Every scene has its own rules.<br><br>- &quot;Bamboo Forest&quot;, &quot;Amusement Park&quot;, and &quot;Mountain Top&quot; have similar rules, and score points by capturing more land, with the player with the highest score winning. They are the standard model.<br> <br>- In Standard mode, weapons that disappear at the end of a turn are marked as active weapons.  The earlier the weapon drops, the higher the priority of their valid mark.  <br><br>-Valid tags with larger sequences are corrupted by valid tags with smaller sequences.<br><br>- Scenes &quot;Castle War&quot; and &quot;Desert&quot; are special rules<br><br>-Castle Wars requires the player's duck knight to snatch an opponent's flag in order to win.<br><br>- &quot;Desert&quot; requires player-controlled birds to avoid obstacles and shoot down opponents' nests to win.<br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2186350/extras/6b41937ec7b14e9a4184f840e23e7b30.poster.avif?t=1681473671\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2186350/extras/6b41937ec7b14e9a4184f840e23e7b30.webm?t=1681473671\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2186350/extras/6b41937ec7b14e9a4184f840e23e7b30.mp4?t=1681473671\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div>",
    "about_the_game": "Throwing Master is a casual competitive game played by two to four players, who make decisions based on the rules of the game and choose their preferred weapon to defeat their opponent.<br><br>- Requires at least 2-4 players to play.<br><br>- Players set the rules of the game, choose the scene to fight.<br><br>- Every scene has its own rules.<br><br>- &quot;Bamboo Forest&quot;, &quot;Amusement Park&quot;, and &quot;Mountain Top&quot; have similar rules, and score points by capturing more land, with the player with the highest score winning. They are the standard model.<br> <br>- In Standard mode, weapons that disappear at the end of a turn are marked as active weapons.  The earlier the weapon drops, the higher the priority of their valid mark.  <br><br>-Valid tags with larger sequences are corrupted by valid tags with smaller sequences.<br><br>- Scenes &quot;Castle War&quot; and &quot;Desert&quot; are special rules<br><br>-Castle Wars requires the player's duck knight to snatch an opponent's flag in order to win.<br><br>- &quot;Desert&quot; requires player-controlled birds to avoid obstacles and shoot down opponents' nests to win.<br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2186350/extras/6b41937ec7b14e9a4184f840e23e7b30.poster.avif?t=1681473671\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2186350/extras/6b41937ec7b14e9a4184f840e23e7b30.webm?t=1681473671\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2186350/extras/6b41937ec7b14e9a4184f840e23e7b30.mp4?t=1681473671\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div>",
